# SFC "traffic light" on stock LinuxCNC HAL: three steps, each held by a step timer.
#
#   traffic_light.sfc - the program in IEC 61131-3 SFC text (what the author writes)
#   traffic_light.clp - the same program as ClassicLadder Grafcet + ladder rungs
#   traffic_light.hal - this file: realtime thread, ClassicLadder, wiring
#
# Runs in plain `halrun` (package linuxcnc-uspace), no LinuxCNC motion, no hardware.

loadrt threads name1=plc period1=1000000          # 1 ms scan

# --- ClassicLadder: sizes are what traffic_light.clp uses, but the HAL pin arrays (s32in, s32out,
# floatin, floatout) are at least 1: with 0 classicladder_rt brings HAL down at the first scan
loadrt classicladder_rt numRungs=7 numBits=4 numWords=0 numTimers=3 numMonostables=0 numCounters=0 numPhysInputs=3 numPhysOutputs=6 numArithmExpr=3 numSections=2 numS32in=1 numS32out=1 numFloatIn=3 numFloatOut=1
addf classicladder.0.refresh plc
loadusr -w classicladder --nogui traffic_light.clp

# VAR_INPUT of the program = ClassicLadder %IF, TIME in milliseconds (live knobs, change with setp)
setp classicladder.0.floatin-00 3000    # t_red
setp classicladder.0.floatin-01 3000    # t_green
setp classicladder.0.floatin-02 1000    # t_yellow

# --- operator / safety inputs ---------------------------------------------------------
net enable     classicladder.0.in-00          # %I0 run permission from the operator
net hold       classicladder.0.in-01          # %I1 Hold: step time pauses, no transitions
net permit     classicladder.0.in-02          # %I2 E-stop chain OK

# --- lamps (program outputs) ----------------------------------------------------------
net lamp-yellow classicladder.0.out-03        # %Q3
net lamp-red    classicladder.0.out-04        # %Q4
net lamp-green  classicladder.0.out-05        # %Q5

# step activity X1..X3 as HAL pins (for halscope, a panel, or another node)
net X1-red    classicladder.0.out-00
net X2-green  classicladder.0.out-01
net X3-yellow classicladder.0.out-02
